[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mdeepseek_deepseek-v4-flash-failing-tests-trial-2[0m[0m
All 15 tests pass. Here's a summary of the 10 bugs fixed across 3 modules:

**`src/auth.py`** — 3 fixes:
- `has_permission`: was doing `required in user_roles` (case-sensitive), now uses `casefold()` for case-insensitive comparison
- `is_admin_or_owner`: was using `and` instead of `or` — a plain user who is the resource owner was denied; an admin who isn't the owner was also denied

**`src/inventory.py`** — 4 fixes:
- `__init__`: mutable default `= {}` caused all no-arg instances to share the same dict; changed to `None` sentinel + fresh copy
- `add`: was overwriting `self._stock[sku]` instead of accumulating (`= qty` → `= .get(sku, 0) + qty`)
- `reserve`: guard `>=` prevented reserving exactly the available stock (`qty > available` instead of `>=`)
- `release`: no validation against negative reserved; added check that `current - qty < 0` raises `ValueError`

**`src/text_utils.py`** — 3 fixes:
- `slugify`: wasn't lowercasing — added `char.lower()` on each alphanumeric char
- `slugify`: `replace("--", "-")` only collapsed single pairs; rewritten to skip consecutive separators inline during character processing
- `truncate`: was appending suffix to full `text[:max_len]`, exceeding the limit; now truncates to `max_len - len(suffix)` before appending suffix
